WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.187 --> 00:00:14.875
"Do you ride with the caravan too?"

2
00:00:15.536 --> 00:00:16.296
asked Mandy.

3
00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.599
"Sometimes," replied Berk.

4
00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.003
"My father and I have traveled the entire empire."

5
00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.285
"That must be fun!"

6
00:00:26.805 --> 00:00:27.526
said Vinnie.

7
00:00:27.546 --> 00:00:31.937
"Most of the time, it is," Berk said, smiling.

8
00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:34.798
They arrived at a coffee shop.

9
00:00:35.838 --> 00:00:38.779
Men were outside sitting and drinking coffee.

10
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.200
The children went in.

11
00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:44.402
Some men were smoking from a big pipe.

12
00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:49.324
Berk gave his father's bag to Hasad, the shop owner.

13
00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:52.465
Hasad gave Berk a bag in return.

14
00:00:53.665 --> 00:00:55.586
Hasad spoke to Berk quietly.

15
00:00:56.827 --> 00:00:59.448
Then a man stood up and raised his hands.

16
00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:01.853
"Time for a story!"

17
00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:03.034
he shouted.

18
00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:06.097
The crowd cheered.

19
00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:09.960
"We are happy to have Duman the storyteller with us!"

20
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.541
the man said.

21
00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:13.643
Everyone clapped.

22
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:19.428
Then, a man wearing a colorful robe stood up in the middle of the shop.

23
00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:25.052
It was Duman the storyteller, and he began to speak.

24
00:01:25.072 --> 00:01:29.096
"Prince Babar wanted to see the world.

25
00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:32.617
His father, the sultan, would not allow him to go.

26
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:36.558
The sultan wanted the prince to stay in the palace and marry.

27
00:01:36.578 --> 00:01:42.859
'But Father,' said the prince, 'I must see our great empire before I marry.'"

28
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.460
Duman pulled out a bright handkerchief.

29
00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.321
He waved it in front of his face.

30
00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:52.082
Then his voice changed.

31
00:01:52.102 --> 00:01:55.683
"'You can see the empire after you marry!'

32
00:01:57.163 --> 00:01:59.504
At that moment, the prince's mother came in."

33
00:02:00.656 --> 00:02:02.697
Duman waved the handkerchief again.

34
00:02:03.918 --> 00:02:07.080
This time his voice was high, like a woman's.

35
00:02:08.421 --> 00:02:11.402
"'Babar! I've found the perfect bride for you.

36
00:02:12.403 --> 00:02:14.144
She looks exactly like me.'"

37
00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:21.888
All the men in the coffee shop laughed loudly.

38
00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.991
"He's doing all the characters himself!"

39
00:02:27.351 --> 00:02:28.252
giggled Mandy.

40
00:02:29.596 --> 00:02:33.239
Berk stopped talking with Hasad and stood next to Vinnie.

41
00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:35.340
"Isn't he funny?"

42
00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:38.462
Vinnie pointed to the storyteller.

43
00:02:39.943 --> 00:02:42.845
Berk smiled, but then suddenly froze.

44
00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:46.507
In fact, everyone stopped laughing.

45
00:02:47.688 --> 00:02:50.310
A group of men wearing uniforms walked in.

46
00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:53.552
They had long swords in their belts.

47
00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:57.615
"We want coffee," demanded one of them.

48
00:02:57.635 --> 00:03:03.049
"You," he said to the storyteller, "Go on with your story."

49
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.111
Duman nervously continued.

50
00:03:06.131 --> 00:03:08.672
"Who are they?"

51
00:03:09.392 --> 00:03:10.492
Vinnie asked Berk.

52
00:03:10.512 --> 00:03:14.154
"The Janissary," explained Berk.

53
00:03:15.254 --> 00:03:17.895
"They used to be slaves from outside the empire.

54
00:03:18.836 --> 00:03:20.576
They're trained to be the best fighters.

55
00:03:21.717 --> 00:03:23.598
The Janissary protect the sultan."

56
00:03:24.978 --> 00:03:26.099
"You, children!

57
00:03:26.559 --> 00:03:27.419
Come over here!"

58
00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:29.160
one guard shouted.

59
00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.337
The children walked over to him.

60
00:03:32.357 --> 00:03:34.057
"Who are you?"

61
00:03:34.577 --> 00:03:35.057
he asked.

62
00:03:35.077 --> 00:03:40.159
"Our caravan just arrived in Istanbul and began Berk.

63
00:03:41.539 --> 00:03:44.620
The guard grabbed Berk's bag and looked inside.

64
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.521
"This bag is full of silver!"

65
00:03:48.081 --> 00:03:48.581
he said.

66
00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:52.162
"Young thieves were seen in the palace this morning."

67
00:03:52.182 --> 00:03:54.463
"I wasn't with them, sir.

68
00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:58.044
That silver is for my father," Berk explained.

69
00:03:59.816 --> 00:04:01.937
"And what do you have in your pockets?"

70
00:04:02.597 --> 00:04:04.457
another soldier asked the children.

71
00:04:05.658 --> 00:04:07.939
Berk and Vinnie had nothing in their pockets.

72
00:04:09.259 --> 00:04:10.239
But Mandy did.

73
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.900
She pulled out her mother's glittering earrings.

74
00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.881
Berk looked at her in shock.

75
00:04:17.401 --> 00:04:18.602
So did the soldiers.

76
00:04:19.702 --> 00:04:22.003
The soldier took the earrings from Mandy.

77
00:04:23.003 --> 00:04:25.584
He held them in his palm and stared at them.

78
00:04:26.597 --> 00:04:29.788
"This jewelry surely does not belong to a little girl!"

79
00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.313
the soldier said.
